{"checkIfIsAvailable calculates both start and end from slotStartTime, so a slot that starts within working hours but ends after workingHour.endTime will be incorrectly marked available": 0.9512261152267456, "checkIfIsAvailable uses === to compare two newly-created Dayjs instances, so an override where start==end is never treated as an all-day override and can incorrectly allow slots that should be blocked": 0.8636888265609741, "When selectedSlots exist, getSchedule calls checkIfIsAvailable without passing workingHours or dateOverrides, so returned availability can ignore normal working hours and date overrides in that code path": 0.8021708726882935, "getSlots computes timezone offsets by parsing override.start.toString(), which depends on the server's local timezone representation and can yield incorrect offsets and thus wrong slot times for date overrides": 0.8871493339538574, "When dateOverrideExist is set to true, the function immediately returns true, skipping the busy times check at the end of the function, causing calendar conflicts to be ignored during date overrides": 0.8967421650886536, "The logic uses find to check if a slot is outside a date override or working hour block. If a user has multiple overrides or working hour blocks on the same day, the slot might be incorrectly marked as unavailable because it falls outside the first evaluated block, even if it fits in another": 0.8416023254394531}